Sample Output (short)
{
  "mode": "movement",
  "level": "beginner",
  "rasa": "none",
  "steps": [
    {
      "id": "S1",
      "posture": "ARA",
      "hand_mudra": "ALA",
      "movement": "TURN_R",
      "beats": "1B",
      "direction": "RIGHT",
      "description": "Execute a controlled pivot to face the right side.",
      "rasa_expression": "none",
      "teaching_note": "Keep the center of gravity low and steady."
    }
  ]
}

More examples are in /examples.

⸻

How it Works

1. Gemini / Google AI Studio
	•	System prompt enforces the NNF format
	•	User input → validated JSON output
	•	Tested on multiple movement + story prompts

2. Opus Workflow

(For hackathon submission)
	•	LLM node generates NNF
	•	Rules validate the structure
	•	Audit artifact logs steps, inputs, confidence, and errors
	•	Output exported (PDF / JSON / sheet)

3. Framer Prototype
	•	Paste JSON into UI
	•	Visual renderer displays steps as glyphs + annotations
	•	Used for user demo

⸻

Why Nrityapath Matters

Classical dance has rich structure but lacks a digital standard for movement representation.

Nrityapath introduces:
	•	a new notation language
	•	AI-assisted choreography
	•	consistent, reusable structure
	•	accessibility for modern learners
	•	a path toward digital archives & creative tools

⸻

🛠️ Setup for Developers

No backend needed yet.
To test:
	1.	Open Framer
	2.	Paste any JSON from /examples
	3.	Visualize choreography instantly

You can also integrate with Gemini API and Opus.

